  partName: Exhaust Manifold (2)
  description: The Exhaust Manifold (2) is a small, thin-flat metal component situated
    at the middle-center-center of the engine, responsible for collecting and directing
    exhaust gases away from the combustion chamber. Its dark metal finish suggests
    a high-temperature resistant material, which is essential for withstanding the
    intense heat generated during the exhaust process. Interestingly, the exhaust
    manifold's design is optimized to minimize backpressure and maximize engine efficiency.
